      equipment: 'Double-six domino set.',
      dealing: 'One player is dealer. Each player receives (8 minus the number of players) tiles. The dealer draws one tile at random from the remainder and turns it face up to start the line. Remaining tiles form the boneyard face down.',
    },
    turnFlow: "Tiles are laid end to end matching suits. Player to dealer's left leads. Each turn: play two tiles (one on each end of the line), or if unable and boneyard not empty draw one tile and pass, or if boneyard empty and one tile left play that tile on either end, or if boneyard empty and cannot play then pass. Anyone may call blocked game; hands are then scored. Round ends when someone dominoes, blocked game is called, or everyone has passed.",
